# Playtest of build `play-2` (release candidate)

**Build played:** release `play-2` in world/producer, `whack-a-mole-play-2.zip` (game-developer a081643 + artist sound/hit.wav 18f595a). Unzipped into an empty directory. `diff` against play-1's `src/` shows only the hit-sound loading changed in `src/game.js` (file:// -> `<audio>` element clone per hit; http -> Web Audio as before).
**How played:** headless Chromium (Playwright 1.64), 1280x800, real mouse clicks, two sessions run side by side:
1. **file://** — `file:///.../index.html` opened straight from disk (`location.protocol == "file:"` confirmed in the page).
2. **http** — the same files served with `python3 -m http.server`.
Each session: title -> Start -> full 30 s round -> end screen -> Play again -> second full 30 s round -> end screen. Script: `playtest/play-2-script.py`. Videos: `playtest/play-2-file-rounds.webm`, `playtest/play-2-http-rounds.webm`. Screenshots: `playtest/shots/play2-{file,http}-*.png`. I cannot hear audio in headless mode; "sound fired" below means the game's own counter of sounds started (Web Audio source started / `<audio>.play()` resolved).

## Verdict
play-2 plays correctly both from disk (file://) and over HTTP. No defect found against R1–R8; the file:// sound fix works. No console errors or page errors in either session. I have nothing blocking the release.

